{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will set My face against that man.</b> If he does not turn back from his wickedness, so that his death not serve as atonement." "<b>And I will cut him off.</b> This must perforce be understood as excision to eternal life, since they have stoned him with stones, so that he cannot be cut off again in this world." "<b>To defile My sanctuary.</b> To remove the Shekhinah from Israel, and it is fitting that they stone him. <b>And to profane My holy name.</b> Therefore I will set My face against him, even though it is not idolatry."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:03.685271876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}